AD  - SVKM's NMIMS, Dept. of CSE(DS), Hyderabad, India
AD  - AI SVKM's NMIMS, Hyderabad, India
AB  - A major barrier in adopting AI diagnostic tools in healthcare is their lack of explainability. As these systems are black boxes in nature, as they fail in showing the logic behind their predictions, it undermines confidence among medical professionals and patients, raising concerns about their dependability. This paper introduces a new Neurosymbolic AI (NeSy) methodological framework that tackles this issue by combining two important components: Deep Neural Network (DNN) and Symbolic Reasoning Engine (SRE). The key objective is to create a hybrid diagnostic model that is transparent and explainable, bringing together the strong pattern recognition abilities of DNNs with the clear, logic-based structure of symbolic AI. The proposed framework uses a Graph Neural Network (GNN) and turns the structured medical Knowledge Graphs (KGs) into useful data, which is then instigated with a Transformer-based model to process the user's reported symptoms. A final attention-based reasoning module applies logical rules to ensure the diagnostic outcome is accurate and provides explanations of how the outcome and the symptom associations hold in a simplified manner so that the user will be able to understand them easily. To test how well does this framework works in real-world settings, it is built into a complete mobile healthcare solution called the "smart diagnostic core". This solution joins the AI system with a user-friendly Android interface and a secure database management system to handle personal health information. By combining a smart diagnostic core with an easy-to-use mobile interface and a secure data system, this work sets a new standard for a trustworthy digital health assistant, showing a real way to build AI that is transparent, explainable, dependable, and centred around the user's needs.  © 2026 IEEE.
