UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105046208184?origin=resultslist
AD  - Delhi Technological University, Dept. Of Computer Science And Engineering, New Delhi, India
AB  - Recent advances in stock market prediction have increasingly leveraged multimodal machine learning by integrating numerical price data with unstructured sources such as news sentiment and social media signals. While these approaches consistently outperform traditional price-only models, they often introduce significant interpretability challenges due to their black-box nature. This systematic review surveys over 20 peer-reviewed studies published between 2023 and 2026, analyzing multimodal prediction models across architectures (Recurrent neural networks, Transformers, and graph-based models), fusion strategies (early, late, and hybrid), and data modalities. We evaluate each category with respect to predictive accuracy, robustness under market volatility, and model explainability. Our findings indicate that Transformer-based models with self-attention mechanisms offer improved interpretability compared to conventional recurrent architectures, though most systems still rely on post-hoc explanation methods such as SHAP or LIME. Based on these insights, we propose the concept of Trustworthy Financial AI, emphasizing the joint optimization of predictive performance and explainability in multimodal financial forecasting models. © 2026 IEEE.
