AB  - The interpretability of deep learning models has gained the attention of many researchers and organisations in recent years. The doctoral research wilwill include the interpretability and explainability of Recurrent Neural Networks (RNN) and its variant architectures.RNNs find extensive application in speech recognition and healthcare, yet their complex architecture often renders them as "black box models". FSA and RNN both handle sequential data, with FSA transitioning between states and RNN updating hidden states at each step. This similarity enables comparing FSA's transitions to RNN's hidden state updates. FSA's graphical representation enhances human understanding. The findings of this study will be used to lead the development of post hoc explanation methods (XAI) for time series data employing deterministic finite state machines as an explainability method. © 2023 CEUR-WS. All rights reserved.
