AB  - The growing demand for trustworthy artificial intelligence (AI) has accelerated research into models that are not only accurate but also interpretable and aligned with causal reasoning. In this regard, we present NeuroSymX, a hybrid neuro-symbolic AI system that combines deep learning and symbolic reasoning to derive transparent, causally consistent and human interpretable decisions. In contrast to classic black box neural networks that are difficult to justify make predictions, or adhere to domain specific rules, NeuroSymX entails the combination of Transformer-LSTM-based neural networks and Prolog-based symbolic logic engines. Causal graphs and ontology-consistent rules are also implemented into the framework based on external ontologies like ConceptNet. Extensive testing done on ten benchmark datasets such as CLEVR, UCI, eICU, and COMPAS show that NeuroSymX has an accuracy of between 85.4-94.9, with fidelity, and causal consistency scores always outperforming both explainable neural and symbolic-only models. NeuroSymX also scored the best in terms of user trust in comparative analysis with an average of more than 4.5 out of 5. Ablation studies also confirmed the relevance of each component and the complete model performed better in every case. Notably, the model allows counterfactual and abductive reasoning, allowing end-users to query the decisions using the question- why and the question- what-if. This makes NeuroSymX an effective solution to sensitive areas like healthcare, legal compliance and finance. The findings confirm the idea that the synergy between symbolic logic and sub-symbolic learning can be used to bridge the gap between AI-based accuracy and transparency, which creates the opportunity to implement explainable and ethical AI at scale. © 2026 IEEE.
