AB  - As financial systems continue to grow more complex and interconnected, they are also becoming more prone to disruption and systemic crises. This paper presents an Adaptive AI Financial Ecosystem which aims at identifying instabilities early before they arise. It uses Graph Neural Networks (GNNs) to represent dynamic interdependencies between banks, fintech platforms, and markets, and timeseries forecasting models to analyse past and current indicators to produce early-warning signals. An agent of Reinforcement Learning (RL) in a Digital Twin simulation environment evaluates and suggests the best policy behavior in changing situations. The techniques of explainable AI (XAI) also provide transparency and regulatory interpretability. The empirical findings indicate that the proposed system is able to achieve an F1-score of 0.82, achieve a 11-day lead time on crises, and a 61 -percent decrease in systemic stress, which is greater than the traditional surveillance methodologies. The results highlight the possibility of adaptive, self-education AI systems to enhance financial stability and build a resilient and data-driven economy. © 2026 IEEE.
