AB  - Although deep learning has improved the classification of brain tumours, available approaches utilize excessive amounts of statistical correlation making them poor generalisers with a lack of mechanistic interpretability. This paper suggests Causal-MT, a Causal-Aware Multimodal Transformer that transforms the diagnostic analysis into focusing on causal mechanisms understanding to pattern recognition. In contrast to conventional fusion methods, Causal-MT uses a structural causal graph to simulate directional relationships between MRI modalities and uses interventional masking to separate genuine biological drivers and imaging artifacts. We also propose a causal representation disentanglement module to decouple robust mechanistic characteristics and scanner-related styles to a great extent, greatly increasing out-of-distribution performance. Furthermore, the framework incorporates a Large Language Model (LLM) to produce natural language reports on the mechanisms of tumor progression underlying it. The experimental results on the BraTS benchmark and external multi-centers have shown that Causal-MT has a competitive segmentation accuracy with better generalization and reliable causal reasoning of clinical decision-making. The experimental results on the BraTS benchmark and external multicenter datasets show that Causal-MT achieves 92.6% segmentation accuracy with improved generalization and reliable causal reasoning. © 2026 IEEE.
